{
  "note": [
    "The Courtyard's fabric (DR-106), built by dev from COURTYARD.metadata.json v5 and its README (2026-09-14). The game: 'the courtyard of an ancient stone edifice ... decayed to the point where it can probably be termed a ruin. Openings lead north and west, and a stairway downward is visible to the south.'",
    "The platform is the README's nominal 11 m by 8.5 m (x -5.5..5.5, z -5.2..3.3); the eye stands at [0, 1.6, 2.6], just inside the stair's top landing. Walls survive 5.5 to 6 m high, the west one collapsed to a 3 m breach onto the West Wing's broken floor; the south side is a low parapet on the cliff edge, so the sea shows over it.",
    "North: the heavy ancient wall is pierced by the later, angular opening to the Plain Hall (x 0..2.2, 2.7 m high), and the hall itself runs north beyond it as a plain modern bay.",
    "South and down (one route): the first tread is below the platform; the first leg descends south through a 1.6 m cut in the cliff edge to a turn 3 m down, and the second turns left -- east -- along the face and on out of sight, as the README has it. The widths agree with the Winding Stair's UP opening (1.6 m).",
    "Heights on the shared datum (day-one sea zero): this platform stands about 43 m up (the Winding Stair's landing +21, the stair 'about 22 m higher'). The sea here is set at -33 below the platform (+10, about day 3) for the base state, which covers days 1 to 5; the painted states for days 6-7 and 8 raise it.",
    "Ruin (2026-09-14): the walls were first built with level tops, and the north seed read as an intact walled yard. The game calls this a ruin and the README asks for 5-8 m of surviving wall with broken silhouettes extending higher locally, so the north wall now has a broken dip west of the Plain Hall opening and a 7.4 m stub beside it, and steps down at its east corner; the east wall has collapsed to 3.2 m near its middle and falls away towards the sea; fallen blocks lie under both breaks."
  ],
